{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0c52b5e9fa3c5908562badbbc1a9ff895266ea12d234b218523ca3003e54c890"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The extension requires a local or Docker-hosted open LLM implementation such as Ollama or LMStudio, running and exposing an API endpoint reachable from Visual Studio."},{"claim_ids":["clm_504f648f05aeb4939c03e141cbaf147f4e77bf628a6adfdeaa346afb6bce4fff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a Visual Studio extension whose commands appear under the Extensions menu (moved there in v1.9.0; earlier versions placed them under Tools)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5aeedf5a8c7c529d4885e79023445d6b7ea0ccb320c4434272c3f4fb81309542"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project ships a docker-compose file and a sample nginx configuration to test an LLM behind an authenticating reverse proxy locally."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6f3de731e7a42cf1e2d117a1297a4837fb3c6feaf2a24000a9af19a720d5fffd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Generated output can overwrite the selected code via an Apply button or be saved to a dynamically named file in the current project folder via a Save button."},{"claim_ids":["clm_90d08d1fb750a1e91da15903c5aefc90e3ad49f24092630935967588041a2201"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Follow-up feature lets users submit additional prompts that build on a prior code generation, sending the follow-up to the LLM for updated results."},{"claim_ids":["clm_94d78c25a498fcad49d89b45d05e174f2926ca8cbac3eeeb0ede5c775f3fdfac"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration options in the Visual Studio Options menu let users set the LLM base URL, choose a model per command, set HTTP request timeouts, and pick the answer language."},{"claim_ids":["clm_95412ace5f12b83315def870104145fffb95a11cfb725736c30c60f80fa8d8e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prompts target multiple languages (C#, Python, Java), reject non-coding requests, and enforce Clean Code principles with raw, comment-free output following Allman-style braces."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a42471615f9e043609df3b25db5a2ac4366448d94b35bb0353c0cced01632b30"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Since v1.13, an optional authentication token setting makes the extension send an Authorization: Bearer header on all LLM API requests; when empty, the header is omitted for backward compatibility."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d496e2732aac8432cfddf70194315f9729284807c5799199f227bdfe490ba9ab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The list of selectable LLM models is obtained by querying Ollama APIs, so users must install needed models beforehand."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fee01852baee4e1725f417e41810c0a20f4a1e2975d17c7605f0b18bc375d17a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Available commands include Refactor code, Generate unit tests, Follow-up, and Document code, which query the configured LLM and show results in a window."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0c52b5e9fa3c5908562badbbc1a9ff895266ea12d234b218523ca3003e54c890","clm_504f648f05aeb4939c03e141cbaf147f4e77bf628a6adfdeaa346afb6bce4fff","clm_5aeedf5a8c7c529d4885e79023445d6b7ea0ccb320c4434272c3f4fb81309542","clm_6f3de731e7a42cf1e2d117a1297a4837fb3c6feaf2a24000a9af19a720d5fffd","clm_90d08d1fb750a1e91da15903c5aefc90e3ad49f24092630935967588041a2201","clm_94d78c25a498fcad49d89b45d05e174f2926ca8cbac3eeeb0ede5c775f3fdfac","clm_95412ace5f12b83315def870104145fffb95a11cfb725736c30c60f80fa8d8e8","clm_a42471615f9e043609df3b25db5a2ac4366448d94b35bb0353c0cced01632b30","clm_d496e2732aac8432cfddf70194315f9729284807c5799199f227bdfe490ba9ab","clm_fee01852baee4e1725f417e41810c0a20f4a1e2975d17c7605f0b18bc375d17a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_66b14ef9a2984a849c024faadd745a0e","id":"pg_262e160ca7d25690bf870e0df0cea517","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/emilianomusso-entwinellm-readme-md-05d11506b780-0e0df0cea517.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_eef50f07ee655226b1f596c57191d43f"],"title":"EmilianoMusso/EntwineLLM/RE